# mix-of-capabilities 04×05 — una proposizione oltre la definizione letta.
# «A smoke detector is a device that senses smoke» e «a carbon monoxide detector is
# a device which detects the presence of carbon monoxide gas» (Wikipedia) sono
# fatti salvati da lezioni vere (sense/2, detect/2). «the presence of X» lega il
# complemento (`state_noun/1`, grammar.p0). Lo scopo («used to prevent») non apre
# piu' l'analisi di progetto (`intent_cue(purpose_of, …)`, intents.p0).
[mock live]
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test the relative clause of a read definition answers its own question]
!timeout 30
> what does a smoke detector sense?
<~ smoke
> what does a carbon monoxide detector detect?
<~ presence of carbon monoxide gas

[test a state noun keeps what it is the state of]
!timeout 30
> a radon detector is a device which detects the presence of radon gas
<~ presence of radon gas

[test a purpose question does not open a design analysis]
!timeout 30
> what is a carbon monoxide detector used to prevent?
<! a workable design
